    "body": "Store non-globstar prefix counts in section records instead of a separate vector, avoiding its allocations during multi-globstar matching. Matching bounds use the same counts; matching behavior and recursion limits are unchanged. Add regression coverage and benchmarks for multi-globstar matching and in-memory path filtering.\n\nMeasured against ea6ec93b2f6504a757660891402872897a2db81a on Apple M2, macOS arm64, Node v27.0.0-pre, V8 15.5.35.22-node.15.\n\nFiltering throughput changes below include unadjusted 95% confidence-interval half-widths. Reverse runs swap baseline and candidate labels.\n\n| Pattern | Path syntax | Candidate vs baseline | Reverse: baseline vs candidate |\n| --- | --- | ---: | ---: |\n| `**/node_modules/**/test/**` | POSIX | +26.57% +/- 1.33% | -20.81% +/- 1.04% |\n| `**/src/**` | POSIX | +11.52% +/- 1.10% | -9.63% +/- 2.40% |\n| `**/node_modules/**/test/**` | Windows | +18.36% +/- 1.47% | -15.96% +/- 1.19% |\n| `**/src/**` | Windows | +12.52% +/- 1.82% | -10.44% +/- 1.64% |\n\nThe 16 multi-globstar hit/miss microbenchmarks improve 18.73-37.88% in the forward comparison, with every gain confirmed in reverse.\n\nAcross 30 configurations, each direction used 30 independent samples per binary: 3,600 samples total. All 20 targeted gains remain significant after Holm correction in both directions; neither direction shows a corrected-significant regression.\n\n",
    "created_at": "2026-10-14T06:12:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-14T07:52:00Z",
